From cf4a8ae38b150307e12d0fe526a4b392165e526d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:26:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_tasks_panel: list only the tasks of this window's
 project
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.51 (ask 75). The panel read one app-wide store,
TaskHistoryStore, and AgentTasksPanel::groups filtered only by status;
the module's own comment said it listed "every task of every window". The
tasks card in the agent panel was already scoped (it follows its own
panel's threads) and is unchanged.

- groups keeps a record when its thread's metadata maps to the window's
  project: agent_ui::thread_organization::list_scope::session_project
  derives the key the way thread_project does for lists per project
  (0123), and the panel compares it with ProjectKey::from_group of its
  project. A thread started with another set of folders is another
  project and is not listed, as in the sidebar (operator, 2026-11-17).
  A record whose thread is gone is hidden: with no thread there is no
  project to list it under (operator, 2026-11-21, over the "Thread no
  longer exists" row the panel showed before). Opened by key -- the
  router other callers use -- such a record still says so.
- "Delete All Archived" counts and deletes, and has_archived offers it,
  only over this project's records. Unscoped, the prompt would count, and
  the store delete, records of projects the window does not show.
- The rows re-filter when the thread metadata store changes (a thread's
  folders become known or change) and on the project's worktree events.
- The project is held as a weak Entity<Project>, passed into new: new
  runs inside the workspace's own update, and groups runs inside it too,
  so neither can read the workspace. `project` moves from dev- to normal
  dependencies (Cargo.lock already listed it).

Tests: multi_window's live-value test now runs in a second window of the
same project and proves a third window's other project is not listed
(its first version passed vacuously: two StopConnections number their
sessions from 1 alike, and the third window had no Agent Tasks panel to
register its card); delete_action_all_archived_spares_another_projects_records;
delete_action_scope_follows_a_thread_that_changes_project. The three
"thread vanished" tests assert the row is hidden and the router's notice.
Fixtures: adopt_orphan_sessions gives each seeded session the thread
metadata a session that ran would have, in the window's folders;
forget_thread and move_thread_to simulate deleting and moving a thread;
notice_of and find_record read the panel and the store, not the rows, so
a cross-window test still reads what another project's panel shows.
Red seen with the scope disabled: those 6 tests failed. agent_tasks_panel
289/289.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
